Show the root of the local file system as the computer in the path bar.

The first segment of a file dialog's location is the file system root, and
GTK gives it the icon of the volume it is on -- drive-harddisk-symbolic, a
square with a hole in it that reads as nothing in particular.  Windows
begins every address with "This PC" and its monitor icon; the local root is
shown that way here (computer-symbolic).  Other roots -- a mounted volume, a
network share -- keep their volume's icon.

